{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":21,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.k3Value_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.k3Value_eq","kind":"theorem","line":234,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.lean#L234-L239","doc":"It is the central scalar `q³ - q⁻³`, exactly as the block states. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.k3Value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.k3Value","kind":"def","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.lean#L231-L232","doc":"The block's narrative object, `σ³ - σ⁻³ = 3h + h³`, as a value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.central_value_unweighted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.central_value_unweighted","kind":"theorem","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.lean#L220-L229","doc":"**A central value passes through the channel average untouched.**  The three\nweights sum to 1, so a quantity every channel agrees on is returned as-is — there\nis no measure factor and in particular no `1/3` on this side. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.classical_point_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.classical_point_iff","kind":"theorem","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.lean#L188-L193","doc":"The same condition in factored form: `q⁴ + 1 = 2q²` is `(q² - 1)² = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.weightRatio_eq_third_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.weightRatio_eq_third_iff","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.lean#L168-L186","doc":"**The deformed weight equals `1/3` EXACTLY at the classical point.**\n`weightRatio q = 1/3 ↔ q⁴ + 1 = 2q² ↔ (q² - 1)² = 0`, i.e. `q² = 1`.\n\nThis is the notation register's own rule made precise for this weight: the\n`q`-deformed and classical measures *coincide at `q = 1` and nowhere else*.  So\nusing `1/3` at the substrate `q₀ ≈ 1.11` is a genuine choice of the classical\nmeasure, not a harmless simplification — and by `weights_at_one` that is the\nPlancherel measure of `S₃`.\n\n(Corrected in authoring: this was first stated as `q⁴ = 2q²`, which is wrong —\n`lean` rejected it.  `3(q⁴+1) = q⁴+4q²+1` gives `2q⁴ - 4q² + 2 = 0`, i.e.\n`(q²-1)² = 0`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.weightRatio_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.weightRatio_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.lean#L162-L166","doc":"**The corpus's `1/3` is this weight at `q = 1`.**  `(1+1)/(1+4+1) = 1/3` —\nplain evaluation, since the denominator is `6 ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.weighted_channel_value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.weighted_channel_value","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.lean#L151-L160","doc":"**The full three-channel weighted value collapses to `weightRatio · R`.**\nThe symmetric and alternating terms cancel because `w_sym = w_alt` and their\nchannel values are exact negatives, leaving the standard term alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.weightRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.weightRatio","kind":"def","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.lean#L147-L149","doc":"The weight the three-channel combination reduces to,\n`(q⁴+1)/(q⁴+4q²+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.channel_alt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.channel_alt","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.lean#L140-L145","doc":"**Alternating channel** `-c/q + d` is `-R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.channel_std","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.channel_std","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.lean#L133-L138","doc":"**Standard channel** `c·z_D + d` is `α·R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.channel_sym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.channel_sym","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.lean#L126-L131","doc":"**Symmetric channel** `c·q + d` at `(c,d) = (2h, -h²)` is `R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.classical_weights_eq_plancherel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.classical_weights_eq_plancherel","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.lean#L121-L124","doc":"**Those are exactly `(f^λ)²/n!`** for `λ ⊢ 3` with `f^λ = 1, 2, 1`, `n! = 6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.weights_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.weights_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.lean#L113-L119","doc":"**At `q = 1` the weights are `1/6, 2/3, 1/6`** — the classical Plancherel\nmeasure of `S₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.weights_sum_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.weights_sum_one","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.lean#L104-L111","doc":"**The three weights are a probability measure**: they sum to 1 for every `q`\nwith `q⁴+4q²+1 ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.wStd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.wStd","kind":"def","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.lean#L101-L102","doc":"`w_std = (q²+1)²/(q⁴+4q²+1)` — the `(2,1)` weight. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.wSym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.wSym","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.lean#L98-L99","doc":"`w_sym = w_alt = q²/(q⁴+4q²+1)` — the `(3)` and `(1³)` weights. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.weightDen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.weightDen","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.lean#L95-L96","doc":"Common denominator of the three substrate weights. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.alphaOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.alphaOf","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.lean#L92-L93","doc":"`α = (q⁴+1)/(q²+1)²`, the augmentation-to-`z_D` ratio. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.symValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.symValue","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.lean#L89-L90","doc":"The `k = 2` reversal value on the symmetric channel, `R = q² - q⁻²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.zD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.zD","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.lean#L86-L87","doc":"The convention-D Markov parameter `z_D = q³/(q²+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.hOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.hOf","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FlavourSplitThreeChannelWeight.lean#L83-L84","doc":"`h = q - q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}